<<<
The sequence change of is should be to was, & were instead ruins the sense; ‘ were to be successful ’ means ‘ succeeded ’ or ‘should succecd °’, not ‘ was to have a chance °.
===
The sequence change of *is* should be to *was*, & *were* instead ruins the sense; 'were to be successful' means 'succeeded' or 'should succecd', not 'was to have a chance'.
>>>

