<<<
submissible, -ittable. The second form is unexceptionable; but on the principle explained in -ABLE 2, submissible would have been expected to establish itself on the analogy of ad, 0, & per, -missible. It is in fact, to judge from the OED, hardly existent, but may nevertheless be recommended as preferable.
===
**submissible, -ittable.** The second form is unexceptionable; but on the principle explained in ^^-ABLE^^ 2, *submissible* would have been expected to establish itself on the analogy of *ad, o,* & *per, -missible*. It is in fact, to judge from the OED, hardly existent, but may nevertheless be recommended as preferable.
>>>

